# Line endings. CLAUDE.md requires these files stay LF, and on Windows that is
# NOT the default: the Git for Windows installer sets core.autocrlf=true system
# wide, which rewrites every text file to CRLF in your working directory on
# checkout. This file overrides that for this repository, for everyone who
# clones it, without anyone having to change a global setting.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text and what is binary; `eol=lf` pins
# the working-copy ending for everything it calls text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files. Marking them stops Git trying to convert or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
